    {
      "wanneer": "2026-10-23T06:27:56+00:00",
      "gebeurtenis": "taal_na_skrywer",
      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'Die naaste karre kom dus reguit na jou toe en jy': Missing AWS comma before 'en jy sien hulle aankom' (two main clauses); 'reguit na jou toe' may also suggest the cars are aimed at you.",
        "fix: [taal] in 'Hulle maak die pad nie veilig nie en die kyk bly jou werk': Missing AWS comma before 'en die kyk bly jou werk' (two main clauses).",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'die kar gly nog 'n ent verder': 'Gly' suggests skidding, but a braking car normally just rolls on for a distance; 'ry nog 'n ent verder' may be meant, but changing it touches the claim, so a person or the writer should decide.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'enigiemand wat te voet op of langs 'n pad is / Iemand wat te voet op o': The study text and the glossary define 'voetganger' with different verbs ('is' and 'beweeg'); one definition per term should be chosen, and that may be a shared definition, so it was not changed.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'moenie in 'n bus of bakkie staan nie': With a bakkie, the danger is usually standing on the back ('agterop 'n bakkie'); making that explicit would sharpen the safety rule but adds detail, so it was flagged rather than changed.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'of voor hom staan nie': It is unclear what standing 'in front of' the driver means inside a vehicle (blocking his view?); the intended meaning cannot be fixed without guessing."
      ]
    },
